Here is the revised function. The changes: dropped comments that restated the code, deleted the commented-out `legacyRate` line, removed the stale TODO, and added a JSDoc block plus a comment on the one non-obvious step.

```javascript
/**
 * Applies tier-based pricing to a cart and records the visit for loyalty.
 *
 * Side effects:
 * - Mutates `user.points` (one point per call, not per item or per order).
 *   Callers must invoke this exactly once per checkout or points will inflate.
 * - Mutates `cart` in place: sets `item.subtotal` on every line item and
 *   scales `cart.total`. The same object is also returned for chaining.
 *
 * Note: `item.subtotal` is populated for display/receipt purposes only.
 * `cart.total` is assumed to already be correct on entry; this function
 * does not recompute it from the subtotals.
 *
 * @param {{ items: Array<{ price: number, quantity: number, subtotal?: number }>, total: number }} cart
 * @param {{ tier: string, points: number }} user
 * @returns {typeof cart} The same cart object, mutated
 */
function applyDiscount(cart, user) {
  user.points += 1;

  for (const item of cart.items) {
    item.subtotal = item.price * item.quantity;
  }

  // Gold members get a flat 10% off the order total. Other tiers currently
  // receive no discount; add further tiers here rather than at call sites
  // so all pricing rules stay in one place.
  if (user.tier === 'gold') {
    cart.total *= 0.9;
  }

  return cart;
}
```

Two things worth your attention:

- **The expired-coupon TODO was removed, not resolved.** The function receives no coupon data, so there is nothing to implement here. If coupons are in scope, that belongs in a tracked ticket or a separate `applyCoupon` step, not a comment that sits in the code indefinitely.
- **The loyalty-point behavior looks like a latent bug.** Awarding a point inside a pricing function means any re-pricing (cart edit, retry, re-render) grants extra points. The JSDoc now warns about it, but the cleaner fix is to move `user.points += 1` to the order-confirmation path.
